நெடு","gloss":"tall"},{"text":"தேர்","lemma":"தேர்","gloss":"chariot"}],"gloss":"tall chariot"},{"surface":"நேமி","parts":[{"text":"நேமி","lemma":"நேமி","gloss":"wheel"}],"gloss":"wheel"},{"surface":"போகிய","parts":[{"text":"போகு","lemma":"போகு","gloss":"go"},{"text":"இய","lemma":"இய","gloss":"past adjectival participle"}],"gloss":"which went"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"இருங்கழி","parts":[{"text":"இரும்","lemma":"இரும்","gloss":"dark"},{"text":"கழி","lemma":"கழி","gloss":"backwater"}],"gloss":"dark backwater"},{"surface":"நெய்தல்","parts":[{"text":"நெய்தல்","lemma":"நெய்தல்","gloss":"blue water lily"}],"gloss":"blue water lily"},{"surface":"போல","parts":[{"text":"போல்","lemma":"போல்","gloss":"resemble"},{"text":"அ","lemma":"அ","gloss":"like"}],"gloss":"like"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"வருந்தின","parts":[{"text":"வருந்தின","lemma":"வருந்தின","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"ளளியணீ","parts":[{"text":"ளளியணீ","lemma":"ளளியணீ","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"பிரிந்திசி","parts":[{"text":"பிரிந்திசி","lemma":"பிரிந்திசி","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"னோளே","parts":[{"text":"னோளே","lemma":"னோளே","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true}],"as_printed":true}],"literal":"To enemies as joy, distressingly / in this manner do they come, O lord of the honey-flowing shore? / As the small-tongued bright bell sounds the Viḷari melody, / the wheel of the tall chariot drawn by swift horses having passed, / like the blue water lily of the dark backwater, / she suffered, the pitiable one, she from whom you separated.","translation":"O lord of the shore where honey flows! Do they return in this manner, causing distress to us and joy to our enemies? Like the blue water lily in the dark backwater, crushed by the wheel of the tall chariot drawn by swift horses, while its small-tongued bright bell rings a mournful Viḷari tune, she, the pitiable one, suffered when you separated from her.","modern":"தேன் பாயும் துறைமுகத்தின் தலைவனே! பகைவர்களுக்கு மகிழ்ச்சியாகவும், எங்களுக்குத் துன்பமாகவும் இருக்கும்படி இப்படி வருவார்களோ? வேகமான குதிரைகள் பூட்டிய நெடிய தேரின் சக்கரம் ஏறிச் சென்றதால், கரிய கழியில் உள்ள நெய்தல் மலர் நசுங்குவது போல, சிறிய நாவைக் கொண்ட ஒளிரும் மணி விளரிப் பண் போல ஒலிக்க, நீ பிரிந்து சென்றதால் அந்தப் பேதை வருந்தினாள்.","explanation":"The friend (தோழி) speaks to the hero (தலைவன்) who has returned from his journey, gently reproaching him for his separation. She asks if it is right to return in a manner that brings joy to their enemies and grief to them. She compares the heroine to a delicate blue water lily in the dark backwater, crushed by the heavy wheel of his swift chariot. As the chariot passes, its small bells ring a mournful tune (Viḷari), mirroring the heroine's sorrow. This poignant imagery from the coastal landscape beautifully conveys the physical and emotional toll of the hero's separation on the fragile heroine.","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"}}